<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/chat/reports">Chat Reports</a> lists messages that staff at your location have reported.
        The menu shows a count when any are open. Use <strong>Open</strong> or <strong>Last 90 days</strong> to filter.
        Admins can also pick the location.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Each report shows">
        <ul>
            <li>Who was reported, who reported it and when, and the reason they gave.</li>
            <li>The message as it was when reported. You never see the rest of the conversation.</li>
            <li>A status: <strong>Open</strong>, <strong>Dismissed</strong> or <strong>Action taken</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Deciding a report">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Dismiss</strong>: the message stays and nothing happens to the person.</li>
            <li><strong>Take action</strong>: choose <strong>Remove the message for everyone</strong>, <strong>Stop … posting in
                chat</strong> for 1 day, 7 days, 30 days or until you lift it, or both. Add a note for other managers if
                you like. Neither person sees it.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            Either way, the person who reported it is told it's been reviewed, but not what was done. Deciding one
            report also closes any other open reports of the same message. A posting ban applies across the
            whole company. The person can still read messages.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote>
            You can't review a report about yourself. Another manager has to. Lift a ban early from
            <strong>Suspended from posting</strong>.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
